On the "links" page at www.nethack.org, you'll find
  http://www.melankolia.net/nethack/nethack.guide.html
for "Absolute Beginner's Guide for NetHack 3.4.1", which used
to appear as a periodic posting to this newsgroup before the
author evidently gave up on it.  It is primarily hints, but does
include a bunch of mild spoilers (like how to use a shop to
recognize scroll of identify).  Even though you aren't using
version 3.4.1 (I hope!) and even if you no longer consider
yourself an absolute beginner, you should probably read it.

> First, at the end of every game (well, at least games where I don't
> die early), I have piles of unidentified wands, potions and scrolls.
> [...]  I've noticed, when watching people online at high
> levels, all their stuff in inventory is IDed... so I'm hoping I'm
> missing something here.

       Well characters who reach high levels will have found
lots and lots of stuff and the players running them might well
be willing to sacrifice some of that stuff for trial and error ID.
(But probably not; it's a poor strategy.)

      One thing you need to figure out is how to determine
whether items are blessed, uncursed, or cursed.  Generally
blessed items work better than uncursed and uncursed work
better than cursed, although not always.  (Trial and error
without knowing the curse/bless status is terrible strategy.)

     When an uncursed scroll of identify is read, it has a small
chance of behaving like a blessed one.  From that, you might
infer that blessed scrolls of identify are superior.

     Another thing you'll need to figure out is how to change
an item from cursed to uncursed (quite a few ways) or from
uncursed to blessed (relatively few ways), and perhaps vice
versa eventually.  Once you work those things out, having an
inventory which contains more ID'd items than unID'd ones
won't be such a mystery.



